WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.600
The safety tests are the kit's own design.

2
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:08.189
They parse every script in the kit and fail
the build on any state-changing command:

3
00:00:08.189 --> 00:00:11.641
write verbs, Invoke Rest
Method, Invoke Web Request,

4
00:00:11.641 --> 00:00:14.600
native programs, file
redirection, and more.

5
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:18.161
Every Graph request must
carry a literal Method GET,

6
00:00:18.161 --> 00:00:20.563
with one exception pinned by a test.

7
00:00:20.563 --> 00:00:23.764
A next link that points at a
host other than the cloud's

8
00:00:23.764 --> 00:00:26.674
own Graph host is refused,
so a token never leaves.

9
00:00:26.674 --> 00:00:30.071
This check passes those tests
without any change to them,

10
00:00:30.071 --> 00:00:32.962
because it reads only
through the kit's data path.

11
00:00:32.962 --> 00:00:35.127
That's the point of a single data path:

12
00:00:35.127 --> 00:00:39.312
a new check inherits the safety
properties instead of re-proving them.

13
00:00:39.312 --> 00:00:42.474
If your check seems to
need its own HTTP call,

14
00:00:42.474 --> 00:00:45.549
it doesn't; add what it
needs to the data path.

15
00:00:45.549 --> 00:00:50.658
And the remediation, the command Microsoft
Learn's existing-tenant page gives to

16
00:00:50.658 --> 00:00:53.860
block soft match, is a write,
so it stays out of the kit,

17
00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:56.350
in the change record the finding opens.
